$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure B: Pd-Catalyzed Negishi
Coupling of Aryl Halides with Secondary Alkylzinc Halides. Procedure A
was used with the following changes: A THF solution of alkyl zinc halide
(1.20 mmol, 1.50-2.50 mL) was slowly added via syringe at room
temperature instead of at 0 °C. tert-Butyl
4-(2-cyanophenyl)piperidine-1-carboxylate [CAS # 256951-72-1].15 (Scheme
2, 1d) Following general procedure B with 2-chloro-benzonitrile (138 mg,
1.00 mmol), (1-(tert-butoxycarbonyl) piperidin-4-yl)zinc iodide solution
(2.64 mL, 1.20 mmol, 0.455 M in THF), and toluene (1.36 mL) at 60 °C for
30 min, the reaction was quenched by saturated ammonium chloride solution
instead of hydrochloric acid (1N). The crude product was purified via the
Biotage SP4 (silica-packed SNAP 25 g; 0-50% ethyl acetate/hexanes) to
provide the title compound as a light yellow solid (260 mg, 91% yield).
The isomeric products were not observed by GC and 1H NMR analysis. m.p.
83-85 °C. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ : 7.62 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.56 (t,
J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.33 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.30 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 4.26
(br s, 2H), 3.12 (tt, J = 12.0, 3.6 Hz, 1H), 2.86 (br t, J = 12.0 Hz,
2H), 1.85 (br d, J = 12.0 Hz, 2H), 1.70-1.56 (m, 2H), 1.48 (s, 9H) ppm.
13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ : 154.4, 148.9, 133.0, 132.9, 126.7, 126.3,
117.7, 111.7, 79.3, 43.8, 40.7 (2C), 32.2 (2C), 28.3 (3C) ppm. IR (neat,
cm-1): 2976, 2934, 2854, 2223, 1695, 1600, 1426, 1366, 1326, 1281, 1235,
1166, 1126, 1064, 1013, 986, 940, 888, 862, 764, 736, 520.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, catalyst ligand prepared and used, Negishi coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Negishi Coupling of Secondary Alkylzinc Halides with Aryl Bromides and
Chlorides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Han, Chong; Buchwald, Stephen L.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
