$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the cross-coupling of
aryl iodides and secondary alkylzinc iodides:
2-(4-(iso-Propyl)phenyl)-4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolane (Table
2, Row 2, Column 3, Entry 1). The general procedure was employed with the
following modification: 30 h reaction time. A white solid (211 mg, 86%)
was isolated by column chromatography (gradient from 93:7 to 90:10
Hex:EtOAc). Mp: 78-80 ºC. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 7.76 (d, J = 7.8 Hz,
2H), 7.25 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 2H), 2.95 (septet, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 1.34 (s,
12H), 1.26 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 6H) ppm. 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 152.5,
135.1, 126.1, 83.7, 34.5, 25.0, 24.0 ppm. 11B NMR (160 MHz, CDCl3) δ:
30.9 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective (>100:1 i-Pr product:n-Pr product), Negishi cross-coupling
reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nickel-Catalyzed Negishi Cross-Coupling Reactions of Secondary Alkylzinc
Halides and Aryl Iodides
