$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Scheme 2 A (GPS2A):
Palladium-Catalyzed Cross-Coupling Reactions of 2-Pyridylzinc Pivalates
with Organic Halides In a dry and argon-flushed Schlenk flask equipped
with a magnetic stirring bar and rubber septum the solid organozinc
reagent was dissolved in the solvent of choice. The organic halide (0.84
equivalents) was added followed by Pd(OAc)2 (2 mol%) and XPhos (4 mol%)
and the mixture was stirred for the given time at the given temperature.
After cooling to room temperature, a saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution (10
mL) was added and the aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc (3 × 20 mL).
The combined organic phases were dried over Na2SO4 and filtered. The
solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure and the crude material was
purified by flash column chromatography. Methyl 4-(pyridin-2-yl)benzoate
(6a) According to GPS2A pyridin-2-ylzinc pivalate (1; 700 mg, 700
mg/mmol, 1.00 mmol) was dissolved in dry THF (2 mL). Methyl
4-chlorobenzoate (143 mg, 0.84 mmol) and Pd(OAc)2 (5 mg, 0.02 mmol) and
XPhos (19 mg, 0.04 mmol) were added and the mixture was stirred for 3 h
at 50 °C. Purification by flash chromatography (silica gel, ihexane /
AcOEt = 3:1). N-(tert-butyl)-4-(pyridin-2-yl)benzamide (6d) According to
GPS2A pyridin-2-ylzinc pivalate (1; 700 mg, 700 mg/mmol, 1.00 mmol) was
dissolved in dry THF (2 mL). 4-Bromo-N-(tert-butyl)benzamide (215 mg,
0.84 mmol) and Pd(OAc)2 (5 mg, 0.02 mmol) and XPhos (19 mg, 0.04 mmol)
were added and the mixture was stirred for 3 h at 50 °C. Purification by
flash chromatography (silica gel, ihexane / AcOEt = 2:1). 6d (190 mg, 89
%) as a pale yellow solid. M.p. (°C): 153 - 155. 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3):
δ 8.71 - 8.69 (m, 1H), 8.06 - 8.02 (m, 2H), 7.83 - 7.79 (m, 2H), 7.77 -
7.73 (m, 2H), 7.29 - 7.21 (m, 1H), 5.99 (s, br, 1H), 1.48 (s, 9H).
13C-NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 166.5, 156.3, 149.8, 141.8, 136.8, 136.1,
127.2, 126.9, 122.6, 120.8, 51.7, 28.9. IR (neat, cm-1): 3309 (w), 2971
(w), 2928 (w), 2361 (w), 2339 (w), 1734 (w), 1634 (s), 1540 (vs), 1465
(m), 1436 (m), 1393 (m), 1366 (m), 1324 (m), 1307 (s), 1217 (s), 1157
(w), 1015 (w), 865 (m), 797 (m), 756 (vs). MS (EI, 70 eV): m/z (%) = 254
(M+, 37), 198 (27), 182 (100), 154 (25). HRMS (C16H18N2O): Calcd.:
254.1419. Found: 254.1411 (M+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
