$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Cross-coupling reaction of 3-iodochromones and
arylzinc bromides A hot oven-dried Schlenk tube was charged with
3-iodochromone (0.5 mmol), NiCl2 (0.03 equiv, 2 mg, 0.015 mmol), PPh3
(0.06 equiv, 7.86 mg, 0.03 mmol), and LiCl (1.5 equiv, 31.5 mg, 0.75
mmol) followed by THF (2 mL). The reaction mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 5 min, arylzinc bromide (1.1 equiv, 0.55 mmol) was added
and stirred at room temperature for one more hour. The reaction mixture
was quenched with 10 % HCl (2 mL), and extracted with ethyl acetate (2 ×
15 mL). The combined ethyl acetate extract was washed with 10 % HCl (5
mL) and brine (5 mL), and dried over anhydrous MgSO4. The organic layer
was concentrated under vacuum to give the crude product. Evaporation of
the solvent in vacuo and purification by column chromatography afforded
the expected cross-coupling products. Cross-coupling product c13, Yield:
88%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Negishi cross-coupling, alternative preparation shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of isoflavones by room-temperature nickel-catalyzed
cross-couplings of 3-iodo(bromo)chromones with arylzincs
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zhang, Zunting; Qiao, Jinfeng; Wang, Ding; Han, Ling; Ding, Ru
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Molecular Diversity (2014), 18(2), 245-251

