$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the cross-coupling of
aryl iodides and secondary alkylzinc iodides:
1-(sec-Butyl)-3-methoxybenzene (Table 2, Row 2, Column 1, Entry 2). The
general procedure was employed with the following modifications: 18 h
reaction time, ether used for extractions during work-up. A colorless
liquid (141 mg, 86%) was isolated by column chromatography (95:5
Hex:Ether). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 7.22 (td, J = 7.6 Hz, 0.9 Hz, 1H),
6.79 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 6.75 (d, J = 0.9 Hz, 1H), 6.73 (dd, J = 2.6 Hz,
0.9 Hz, 1H), 3.81 (s, 3H), 2.58 (app. sextet, J = 7.1 Hz, 1H), 1.60 (m,
2H), 1.24 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H), 0.84 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H) ppm. 13C NMR (125
MHz, CDCl3) δ: 159.7, 149.6, 129.3, 119.7, 113.2, 110.8, 55.2, 41.9,
31.2, 22.0, 12.4 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective (>100:1 s-Bu product:n-Bu product), Negishi cross-coupling
reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nickel-Catalyzed Negishi Cross-Coupling Reactions of Secondary Alkylzinc
Halides and Aryl Iodides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Joshi-Pangu, Amruta; Ganesh, Madhu; Biscoe, Mark R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2011), 13(5), 1218-1221

