$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Heteroarylation of Azine
N-Oxides: To a solution of azine N-oxide (1.5 mmol, 150 mol%) and
2-bromopyridine (1 mmol) in THF (10 mL/g) was added
tetramethylpiperidinylzinc chloride lithium chloride complex (1.5 mmol,
150 mol%, TMPZnCl.LiCl 0.69 M in THF). A thin slurry formed after 1-2
minutes. The slurry was sparged with N2 bubbles for 2 minutes and a
degassed slurry of
dichloro-1,1'-[bis(diphenylphosphino)ferrocene]palladium.CH2Cl2 (1.0-3.5
mol %) in THF (1 mL) was added. The resulting tan-orange slurry was then
heated at 60 °C for 18 h. The deep red reaction mixture was cooled to rt
and quenched with saturated aqueous NH4Cl (2 mL) and diluted with 50%
aqueous acetonitrile (2 mL). The solution was extracted with
dichloromethane (2 × 10 mL), dried with Na2SO4 and concentrated. The
residue was purified by chromatography and the combined fractions were
concentrated to afford the desired product. Purifications of biaryl
products were performed using one of the following chromatographic
protocols: Method A: Isco amine Gold column with a gradient of 0-100%
EtOAc/hexanes Method B: Isco amine Gold column with a gradient of 0-10%
MeOH/dichloromethane Method C: Isco C18 column with a gradient of 5-50%
CH3CN in water Method D: SiliaSepTM HP 25 g with a gradient of 10-100%
EtOAc/hexanes/1% Et3N Method C: Isco C18 column with a gradient of 5-50%
CH3CN in water 3-Fluoro-2-(pyridin-2-yl)pyridine 1-oxide (2).
Purification according to method C.
4-Chloro-3-methoxy-2-methyl-6-(pyridin-2-yl)pyridine 1-oxide (15).
Purification according to method B. Tan solid, 85% yield. mp = 80-81°C,
1H NMR δ 8.80 (d, 1H, J = 8 Hz), 8.67 (m, 1H), 8.08 (s, 1H), 7.77 (m,
1H), 7.30 (m, 1H), 3.88 (s, 3H), 2.54 (s, 3H); 13C NMR δ 151.9, 149.41,
149.38, 147.1, 144.7, 136.3, 126.1, 125.4, 125.0, 124.3, 61.4, 12.3. HRMS
calcd for C12H12ClN2O2 [M+H]= 251.0582, found: 251.0582.
